# {{PROJECT_NAME}} — Org Chart

The company that builds {{PROJECT_NAME}}. Seven groups, each an **ownership lane**; four repos, each a
**code location**. They deliberately do not map 1:1 — App Builder and App Publisher share one repo but
never share a write surface.

## The invariant that makes this work

> **Single writer.** Every file surface has exactly one owning role. If two roles can write the same
> file, one of them is wrong and the org has a defect.

This is not a norm, it is a checkable property. `company/check-org.mjs` fails if two roles declare
overlapping `owns` globs. Run it after editing any charter.

## Groups

### 1 · Design System — repo `{{DS_REPO}}`
The source of truth for how {{PROJECT_NAME}} looks. Publishes; never consumes.

| Role | Owns | Never |
|---|---|---|
| `ds-steward` | tokens, variables, collections, modes | screen layout |
| `component-designer` | Figma components + variants | screens, tokens |
| `brand-designer` | identity, logo, brand expression | product UI |
| `design-system-engineer` | the coded mirror (`{{COMPONENT_LIB}}`) + Storybook | Figma authoring, app screens |
| `ds-publisher` | library publication + version/changelog | design authoring |

`design-system-engineer` writes code in `{{ENGINEERING_REPO}}` but reports to this group — its entire
discipline is Figma parity, and its output is consumed by **both** the prototype and the app. Grouping
it with engineering would hide that second consumer.

