| `orchestrator` | decomposition, routing, tracker truth | doing the work it routes |
| `chief-product-officer` | vision, principles, north star, go/no-go | specs, pixels, code |
| `product-manager` | PRD, backlog, prioritization, sprints | strategy, design |
| `business-analyst` | market/competitive research, KPIs, risk | product decisions |

### 3 · Studio — repo `{{STUDIO_REPO}}`
| Role | Owns | Never |
|---|---|---|
| `product-designer` | validated screens; coordinates ux + ui | components, code |
| `ux-designer` | flow spec + acceptance criteria | pixels |
| `ui-designer` | Figma screen build | component internals |
| `ux-writer` | all user-facing copy + localization · **owns the language gate** | layout |
| `art-director` | visual direction, layout, imagery | component specs, motion |
| `motion-designer` | transitions, micro-interactions, gestures, haptics, reduced-motion | building it, motion tokens |
| `flow-reviewer` | independent heuristic + WCAG evaluation (read-only) | building anything |
| `behavioral-scientist` | behavior design, habit + ethics review | UI decisions |
| `data-analyst` | usability evidence, study analysis | product scope |
| `consumer-migrator` | migration of screens onto new DS versions | new design |

### 4 · App Builder — repo `{{ENGINEERING_REPO}}`
| Role | Owns | Never |
|---|---|---|
| `developer` | the {{APP_KIND}} — screens, nav, storage, native modules | components, builds, submission |
| `qa-engineer` | test scenarios, regression baseline, the pre-publish gate | fixing what it finds |

One `developer` covers {{PLATFORM_TARGETS}} because it is one codebase — a platform split would
create a handoff for what is a single file change. Platform *verification* is real and belongs to
`qa-engineer`, which owns the matrix.

### 5 · App Publisher — repo `{{ENGINEERING_REPO}}`
| Role | Owns | Never |
|---|---|---|
| `release-engineer` | build, signing, versioning, artifact provenance, submit | app code, store copy |
| `store-manager` | listing fields, assets, release notes, track promotion | writing marketing copy, the binary |

Same repo as App Builder, different write surface: `release-engineer` owns build + release config,
`developer` owns `src/`. Neither touches the other.

### 6 · Marketing — repo `{{GROWTH_REPO}}`
| Role | Owns | Never |
|---|---|---|
| `marketing-lead` | positioning, GTM, ASO, campaigns, **all store listing copy** | in-app copy (`ux-writer`) |
| `creative-director` | video concept, narrative, direction | writing localized copy |
| `motion-editor` | motion compositions, renders, social asset production | narrative decisions |

**Store listing copy has exactly one author: `marketing-lead`.** `store-manager` publishes it,
`creative-director` illustrates it. This resolves a three-way collision that existed before.

### 7 · Operations — repo `{{GROWTH_REPO}}`
| Role | Owns | Never |
|---|---|---|
| `support-lead` | store reviews, crash triage, feedback → backlog | prioritization (`product-manager`) |
| `compliance-officer` | privacy policy, data-safety + App Privacy declarations, policy review | shipping decisions |
| `growth-analyst` | funnels, retention, activation, experiments | usability evidence (`data-analyst`) |
| `finance-ops` | budget, account + service costs, monetization mechanics | pricing strategy (`cpo`) |

## Routing

`orchestrator` decomposes a goal and names an owner per piece. It **cannot dispatch** — a subagent
cannot spawn subagents. Dispatch happens one of two ways:

- **Main thread** — you or the assistant launch each agent per the routing plan.
- **Workflow** — `{{STUDIO_REPO}}/.claude/workflows/*.mjs` dispatches deterministically, with gates between phases.

Use a workflow when the work fans out (many screens, many checks). Use the main thread when the work
is sequential and each step informs the next.

## Scaling down

Not every project needs 27 roles. `project.config.yaml` → `org.groups` enables groups per project:

```yaml
org:
  groups: [design-system, leadership, studio, app-builder, app-publisher, marketing, operations]
```

A design-only engagement drops `app-builder`, `app-publisher`, `operations`. A solo prototype might run
`design-system` + `studio` alone. Disabled groups render no agents and no commands.
